      37/   0 :                         
      38/   0 :                         ; 1 = interrupt driven receive (RST 6.5 unmasked)
      39/   0 :                         ; 0 = polled only: RST 6.5 stays masked.  Use 0 to find out whether the
      40/   0 :                         ;     interrupt hardware is what is blocking the keyboard.  Keys are still
      41/   0 :                         ;     read whenever a program waits for one; characters typed while BASIC is
      42/   0 :                         ;     busy printing or running are lost.
      43/   0 : =1H                     USEIRQ      EQU 1
