     301/ 1EA :                         ; Drain the receiver into the ring buffer. Reading status clears the
     302/ 1EA :                         ; chip's IRQ flag, so EVERY status read must be followed by draining RDRF
     303/ 1EA :                         ; or a byte can be stranded with no interrupt pending.
     304/ 1EA : DB 15                   SERSVC: IN   ACIA_STATUS
     305/ 1EC : 32 35 80                        STA  SSTAT
     306/ 1EF : E6 08                           ANI  08H                ; RDRF
     307/ 1F1 : C8                              RZ
     308/ 1F2 : DB 14                           IN   ACIA_DATA
     309/ 1F4 : 4F                              MOV  C,A
     310/ 1F5 : FE 03                           CPI  03H                ; Ctrl-C: flag it, don't buffer it
     311/ 1F7 : C2 02 02                        JNZ  SRX1
     312/ 1FA : 3E 01                           MVI  A,1
     313/ 1FC : 32 3C 80                        STA  BRKFLG
     314/ 1FF : C3 EA 01                        JMP  SERSVC
