(1)  194/ 61E :                         ; ---- interrupt handlers --------------------------------------------------
(1)  195/ 61E :                         ; A SETISR handler is a BASIC statement (or several, separated by :) kept as
(1)  196/ 61E :                         ; text.  It runs at a safe point: before the next statement of a running
(1)  197/ 61E :                         ; program, or while BASIC waits for a key at the prompt or in INPUT.
(1)  198/ 61E :                         ; ISRPOLL runs the handler of the lowest pending IRQ, then returns.
(1)  199/ 61E : 3A E2 80                ISRPOLL:LDA  ISRBUSY
