(1)  665/ 9C3 :                         ; ---------------- interrupts: SETISR / CLRISR ----------------
(1)  666/ 9C3 :                         ; SETISR irq,line          handler is  GOSUB line
(1)  667/ 9C3 :                         ; SETISR (statement, irq)  handler is any statement(s), e.g.
(1)  668/ 9C3 :                         ;                          SETISR (PRINT "IRQ RAISED", 2)
(1)  669/ 9C3 :                         ; The handler runs as soon as BASIC is at a safe point (even at the prompt)
(1)  670/ 9C3 :                         ; and ends with the end of its text, or RETURN if it GOSUBs.
(1)  671/ 9C3 :                         ; IRQ 3 (serial card) can be used only when the serial port is NOT the
(1)  672/ 9C3 :                         ; console, IRQ 5 (keyboard/display card) only when it is not; their handlers
(1)  673/ 9C3 :                         ; run when a character arrives (read it with INKEY).
(1)  674/ 9C3 :                         S_SETISR:
(1)  675/ 9C3 : CD 21 13                        CALL SKIPSP
(1)  676/ 9C6 : FE 28                           CPI  '('
